      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Encapsulation",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Encapsulation",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "FyFYfTO6MR9qiVv70zMlo",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 13273.526251340085,
      "y": 7912.6105795579315,
      "width": 1062.91943359375,
      "height": 50,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b6J",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 734126639,
      "version": 48,
      "versionNonce": 815180495,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1786767623923,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Encapsulation means keeping an object’s data private and letting the object control how that data is used. \nYou interact with it through simple methods instead of reaching in and changing its internal details yourself.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Encapsulation means keeping an object’s data private and letting the object control how that data is used. \nYou interact with it through simple methods instead of reaching in and changing its internal details yourself.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "cBzFLSTI7rqa4gzYFvYOg",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 13266.526698720532,
      "y": 7995.624174660631,
      "width": 114.03990173339844,
      "height": 25,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b6K",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 877807919,
      "version": 13,
      "versionNonce": 846256815,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1786767717641,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Abstraction",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Abstraction",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "pQ30lppuSGrNraFjk6UYQ",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 13272.537270941117,
      "y": 8033.455969386491,
      "width": 1047.819091796875,
      "height": 50,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b6L",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1890703201,
      "version": 47,
      "versionNonce": 343364431,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1786767733498,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Abstraction means exposing only what's essential and hiding implementation details behind clear interfaces. \nYou define what something can do without revealing how it does it.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Abstraction means exposing only what's essential and hiding implementation details behind clear interfaces. \nYou define what something can do without revealing how it does it.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "ZCXLH47bCRX7aBHLdHBEi",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 13273.50731695973,
      "y": 8114.252912410389,
      "width": 1597.918701171875,
      "height": 200,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b6M",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 2006693057,
      "version": 32,
      "versionNonce": 1977333601,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1786768026867,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Polymorphism\n\nPolymorphism is what replaces if (type == \"credit\") or switch (vehicleType) statements. \nInstead of checking types, you call the same method and let each object handle itself. \nDifferent objects respond to the same action in their own way.\n\nPython doesn't support compile-time polymorphism because it is dynamically typed. \nMethod names must be unique within a class, and function selection based on argument types cannot be done at compile time since types are only known at runtime.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Polymorphism\n\nPolymorphism is what replaces if (type == \"credit\") or switch (vehicleType) statements. \nInstead of checking types, you call the same method and let each object handle itself. \nDifferent objects respond to the same action in their own way.\n\nPython doesn't support compile-time polymorphism because it is dynamically typed. \nMethod names must be unique within a class, and function selection based on argument types cannot be done at compile time since types are only known at runtime.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "9EGaHH2Ou6CjFHEfwHZAD",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 13272.931787264473,
      "y": 8340.268993378426,
      "width": 454.379638671875,
      "height": 50,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b6N",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 287962735,
      "version": 150,
      "versionNonce": 1619037121,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1786768024309,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Inheritance\n- Safer Alternative is composition + interfaces",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Inheritance\n- Safer Alternative is composition + interfaces",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "rQYx8oUVey-cc-AdFPuLf",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 13266.526698720536,
      "y": 8425.749077229015,
      "width": 1363.63916015625,
      "height": 50,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b6O",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 2129459873,
      "version": 4,
      "versionNonce": 1132645857,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1786771122386,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Python supports multiple inheritance by allowing a class to inherit from multiple base classes. \nWhen there is ambiguity about which method to call, Python uses the MRO, calculated using C3 linearization, to determine the lookup order.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Python supports multiple inheritance by allowing a class to inherit from multiple base classes. \nWhen there is ambiguity about which method to call, Python uses the MRO, calculated using C3 linearization, to determine the lookup order.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    }
  ],
